UAE in 60 Seconds · History in 60 Seconds series · Silkscreen Travel Poster style

Picture: drawn in code (Canvas 2D). Print engine engine/silk.js from the Lemo-Opuscar library (MIT).
Landmarks (round stone tomb, copper ingots, mosque, carrack, coastal fort and wind tower, pearling dhow and oyster,
offshore platform, seven palms, needle tower, skyline, probe) are original stylised silhouettes drawn as simple paths,
not traced from photographs. No logos, no flags, no maps or borders.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts in fonts/):
  Big Shoulders Display — Patric King / Google Fonts
  Outfit — Rodrigo Fuenzalida / Google Fonts

Voice: Kokoro-82M v1.0 (hexgrad, Apache-2.0) via kokoro-onnx, voice bm_george. Checked with faster-whisper (MIT), model base.en.

Music (original score, music/compose.py): an oud-like plucked lute by physical modelling (core/audio/pluck.py, Lemo-Opuscar, MIT);
darbuka, frame drum and ney flute synthesised in code. No samples.
Sound (mix.py): paper swish, stamps, wind, birds, waves, gulls, timber creaks, gas roar, city hum: synthesised in code.
Mastering: FFmpeg (LGPL/GPL) via imageio-ffmpeg.

Facts and sources: FACTS.md.
